# Copy this file to ".env" (same folder as manage.py) and fill it in.
# ".env" is private: .gitignore keeps it out of git. Never share the key or paste it anywhere public.
# A real environment variable, if you set one, wins over what is written here. A blank value is ignored.
# Every line below starts with "#", so copying this file unchanged changes nothing.

# Your free OpenRouteService key (sign up at https://openrouteservice.org/dev/#/signup).
# Paste it after the "=", with no quotes and no spaces. With a key the app plans TRUCK routes by itself.
# Without one it still runs, but only with CAR routes from the free OSRM server, and the page says so.
# ORS_API_KEY=paste-your-key-here

# Optional: force one engine. "osrm" gives car routes even when there is a key. You don't need this line.
# ROUTING_ENGINE=osrm

# The truck, in metres and metric tonnes (these are the defaults: a US tractor-trailer, 80,000 lb).
# TRUCK_HEIGHT_M=4.11
# TRUCK_WIDTH_M=2.59
# TRUCK_LENGTH_M=22
# TRUCK_WEIGHT_T=36.3
